          ],
          "title": "Database Size Growth",
          "type": "timeseries",
          "description": "**What it measures:** Total size of each database in bytes, tracked over time to show growth trends.\n\n**How collected:** `postgres_exporter` queries `pg_database_size()` function which returns size in bytes per database.\n\n**Why it matters:** Unexpected growth spikes can indicate a runaway job inserting data, missing delete/archival processes, or a data leak. Predictable growth helps capacity planning.\n\n**Best practice:** Combine with tablespace-level breakdown to identify which tables are growing fastest. Alert when growth rate exceeds 3× the 30-day average daily growth.\n\n**Also monitor:** Table bloat from unvacuumed dead tuples in PostgreSQL — the table file grows even without new data.",
          "interval": "1m"
        }
      ]
